* {{audio|en|En-us-melancholy.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} [[black bile|Black bile]], formerly thought to be one of the four "cardinal [[humours]]" of animal bodies.
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2001|page=148|passage='''Melancholy''', cold and dry, thick, black, and sour,{{...}}is a bridle to the other two hot humours, blood and choler, preserving them in the blood, and nourishing the bones.}}
# Great [[sadness]] or [[depression]], especially of a thoughtful or introspective nature.
