# {{lb|en|ergative}} To change (or to be changed) from a solid state to a liquid state, usually by a gradual heat.
#: {{ux|en|I '''melted''' butter to make a cake.}}
#: {{ux|en|When the weather is warm, the snowman will disappear; he will '''melt'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To [[dissolve]], [[disperse]], [[vanish]].
#: {{ux|en|His troubles '''melted''' away.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2008|month=October|author=Davy Rothbart|title=How I caught up with dad|journal=w:Men's Health|volume=23|issue=8|issn=1054-4836|page={{gbooks|VMgDAAAAMBAJ|110|melted}}|passage=I gave him a couple of Advil and, after a few minutes, urged him back onto the track. Over the next few laps his pained expression slowly '''melted''', although he still shuffled with a slight limp.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive|figurative}} To [[soften]], as by a warming or kindly influence; to relax; to render gentle or susceptible to mild influences; sometimes, in a bad sense, to take away the firmness of; to weaken.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|IV|iii|passage=Thou would'st have {{...}} '''melted''' down thy youth.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1687|author=w:John Dryden|title=A Song for Cecilia's Day
|passage=For pity '''melts''' the mind to love.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XXI|35|The traveller hears me now and then,<br>⁠And sometimes harshly will he speak:<br>⁠‘This fellow would make weakness weak,<br>And '''melt''' the waxen hearts of men.’}}
#* {{RQ:Bramah Eyes of Max Carrados|passage=He was very dubious at first, but I believe the fellow is genuine in his attachment to the house. His final scruple '''melted''' when he learned that I should not require him to sit up with me.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[discourage]]d.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figurative}} To be emotionally softened or [[touched]].
#: {{ux|en|She '''melted''' when she saw the romantic message in the Valentine's Day card.}}
#: {{ux|en|My heart '''melted''' when I first heard the song.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial}} To be very hot and [[sweat]] [[profuse]]ly.
#: {{ux|en|I need shade! I'm '''melting'''!}}

