#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Tory Frost|title=Going the distance: breaking through the boredom barrier|work=w:The Guardian|date=2013-10-07|url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/the-running-blog/2013/oct/07/distance-boredom-barrier-beginner-runner|passage=Seasoned runners speak wistfully of getting in the zone, of running as '''meditation''' or going into autopilot, powering through the miles.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160329210855/https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/the-running-blog/2013/oct/07/distance-boredom-barrier-beginner-runner}}
