###* {{RQ:Dickens Barnaby Rudge|chapter=11|page=297|passage=The very furniture of the room seemed to '''mellow''' and deepen in its tone; the ceiling and walls looked blacker and more highly polished, the curtains of a ruddier red; the fire burnt clear and high, and the crickets in the hearth-stone chirped with a more than wonted satisfaction.}}
