===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|mantel}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mæntel}}, {{m|ang|mentel|t=sleeveless cloak}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mantel}}; later reinforced by {{der|en|xno|mantel}}, both from {{der|en|la|mantellum|t=covering, cloak}} ({{cognate|fr|manteau}}), diminutive of {{m|la|mantum}} ({{cognate|es|manto}}), probably from {{der|en|cel-gau|*mantos}}, {{m|cel-gau|*mantalos||trodden road}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*mantos}}, {{m|cel-pro|*mantlos}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*menH-||tread, press together; crumble}}. Compare {{cog|is|möttull}}. {{doublet|en|manteau}}.

