#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Know, oh prince, that between the years when the oceans drank Atlantis and the gleaming cities, and the years of the rise of the Sons of Aryas, there was an Age undreamed of, when shining kingdoms lay spread across the world like blue '''mantles''' beneath the stars|year=1932|month=December|title=w:Weird Tales|chapter={{wsource|The Phoenix on the Sword}}|author=w:Robert E. Howard}}
# {{lb|en|malacology}} The [[body]] [[wall]] of a [[mollusc]], from which the [[shell]] is [[secrete]]d. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* '''1990''', Daniel L. Gilbert, William J. Adelman, John M. Arnold ([[editors]]), ''Squid as Experimental Animals'', page 71:
#*: He grasps the female from slightly below about the mid-mantle region and positions himself so his arms are close to the opening of her '''mantle'''.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Danna Staaf|title=Squid Empire|edition=|publisher=ForeEdge|year=2017|isbn=9781611689235|page=8|passage=Molluscan bodies are broadly divided into two parts: a muscular foot and a shell-secreting '''mantle'''.}}
